{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"de0b621f4348ab2ceeacbfff43022dbcd1da01619e96a9ad66652b8c282a3ad0","digest":{"component_or_area":"reducer cache","key_entities":["src/rebar/reducer/_cache.py","src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py","write_cache","process_create","rebar._store.fsutil.atomic_write",".cache.json.tmp",".cache.json","reduce_ticket"],"problem_keywords":["concurrent cache writers","cache coherency","atomic publication","stale state","reducer cache","race condition","file descriptor mutation"],"propositions":["Concurrent reducer cache writers using a fixed .cache.json.tmp artifact can mutate the file after one writer renames it into place, causing stale state to be published under a current-generation hash.","Cache invalidation fails when concurrent reductions of different event generations splice fields from independently valid envelopes, violating the atomic write contract and event-sourced determinism invariant.","Both write_cache in _cache.py and corrupt-CREATE handling in _processors.py publish cache state independently through fixed-temp pathnames instead of a shared atomic mechanism.","A reduction observing stale cached state returns the wrong state without replay, producing false cache hits that break the coherency guarantee."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787486469063467001,"uuid":"40e3daf1-46a4-4a37-bee0-64a1223ee948"}